IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa11-part16-ch2-public`

-- coa11-tests-ch2-public.l4: tests for coa11-part16-ch2-public.l4 (ss 489 to 491).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, before the run.  The assertions for
-- ss 489A, 489B, 489C, 490 and 490A repeat the hand-derived expectations of coa11-tests-ch2-private.l4 for the parallel
-- sections 485A, 485B, 485C, 486 and 486A (the public company text reads the same there, apart from the points the lines
-- below say), with the section numbers changed; the assertions for ss 489(1) to (5), 490(2) and 491 are written afresh.
-- Argument order is the order of the function's GIVEN.  A #TRACE prints FULFILLED or BREACH and cannot be asserted on the
-- stable binary; the expected outcome of each trace is written beside it and was read off the printed result by hand.

§ `Tests: Part 16 Chapter 2, public companies`

§§ `s 489(1): an auditor must be appointed for each financial year`

-- arguments: public company, directors resolved no auditor on the ground audited accounts unlikely, resolution reasonable
#ASSERT `s 489(1) an auditor or auditors of the public company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(1) an auditor or auditors of the public company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "unless the directors reasonably resolve otherwise"
#ASSERT `s 489(1) an auditor or auditors of the public company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- a resolution that is not reasonable does not excuse
#ASSERT `s 489(1) an auditor or auditors of the public company must be appointed for the financial year` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a public company: section 485 is the private company rule

§§ `s 489(2): before the end of the accounts meeting`

-- arguments: the company's first financial year, the day the accounts meeting ended, the day the appointment is made
#ASSERT `s 489(2) the appointment is made before the end of the accounts meeting` FALSE (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 20 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the day the meeting ended: the time of day is not modelled
#ASSERT `s 489(2) the appointment is made before the end of the accounts meeting` FALSE (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 21 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 489(2) the appointment is made before the end of the accounts meeting` FALSE (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- earlier
#ASSERT `s 489(2) the appointment is made before the end of the accounts meeting` TRUE (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 21 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING  -- the first financial year: not covered

§§ `s 489(3) to (5): who may appoint`

#ASSERT `s 489(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not covered
-- s 489(4) arguments: (a) at an accounts meeting, (b) failed at an accounts meeting, (c) directors failed, section 282 answer
#ASSERT `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING  -- not an ordinary resolution
#ASSERT `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING  -- section 282 not known
-- s 489(5) arguments: in accordance with 489, in accordance with 490 or 490A
#ASSERT `s 489(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "may only be appointed"

§§ `s 489A: public interest entities with audit committees`

-- s 489A(1),(2) arguments: under 485(4), private, public interest entity, audit committee, Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General"
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a public interest entity: a scope limit, not covered
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no audit committee (section 489B applies instead)
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- public interest entity not known
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not an appointment under section 489(4)
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a private company (section 489A is the public company rule)
#ASSERT `s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an Auditor General: the flat negative holds whatever else is unknown
-- s 489A(3): the two steps before the appointment (traces: ten days to the appointment)
-- expected: committee recommends on day 3 -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 489A(3)(a) the audit committee must make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 489A the audit committee` DOES `s 489A(3)(a) make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment` AT 3
-- expected: nothing done by day 11 -> BREACH BY the audit committee
#TRACE `s 489A(3)(a) the audit committee must make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- expected: the directors propose on day 10 (the last day) -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 489A(3)(b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 489A the directors` DOES `s 489A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment` AT 10
-- expected: the directors act on day 11 -> BREACH BY the directors
#TRACE `s 489A(3)(b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 489A the directors` DOES `s 489A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment` AT 11
-- the same duties as a decision (arguments: appointment made, committee before, directors before)
#ASSERT `s 489A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 489A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 489A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- the appointment has not been made: the time has not run
-- s 489A(4) and (7): arguments: section 489A(1) answer, small or medium sized enterprise, re-appointment recommended and agreed
-- s 489A(4) and (7): arguments: section 489A(1) answer, SME, reduced market capitalisation, re-appointment recommended and agreed
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "unless the company is (a) a small or medium sized enterprise"
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "(b) a company with reduced market capitalisation"
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- subsection (7)
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the section does not apply (an Auditor General)
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not covered
#ASSERT `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- reduced market capitalisation needs no selection procedure whether or not the section applies
-- s 489A(5): arguments: first and second choice, reasons, free from third party influence, no Article 16(6) term, re-appointment agreed
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (a) missing
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (b) missing
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (c)(i) missing
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (c)(ii) missing
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- subsection (7): (a) and (b) fall away on a re-appointment both agree on
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- but (c) still applies
#ASSERT `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 489A(6): arguments: includes the recommendation, departs from the preference, includes candidates drawn from the procedure, includes reasons
#ASSERT `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- follows the committee: (b) does not bite
#ASSERT `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- departs: (b)(ii) reasons missing
#ASSERT `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- departs: (b)(i) recommendation missing
#ASSERT `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (a) the recommendation not included
#ASSERT `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 489B: public interest entities without audit committees`

#ASSERT `s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- the company has an audit committee (section 489A applies instead)
#ASSERT `s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a public interest entity
#ASSERT `s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- audit committee not known
#ASSERT `s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- expected: the directors propose on day 4 -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 489B(3) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 489B the directors` DOES `s 489B(3) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment` AT 4
-- expected: day 11 reached with no proposal -> BREACH BY the directors
#TRACE `s 489B(3) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
#ASSERT `s 489B(3) the directors proposed an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489B(3) the directors proposed an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 489B(3) the directors proposed an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 489B(4),(5): arguments: section 489B(1) answer, small or medium sized enterprise, proposal is to re-appoint
-- s 489B(4),(5): arguments: section 489B(1) answer, SME, reduced market capitalisation, proposal is to re-appoint
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (a) small or medium sized enterprise
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (b) reduced market capitalisation
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- subsection (5): a proposal to re-appoint the existing auditor
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the proposed auditor or auditors are drawn from the selection procedure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the proposed auditor or auditors are drawn from the selection procedure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not drawn from it
#ASSERT `s 489B(4) the proposed auditor or auditors are drawn from the selection procedure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no procedure

§§ `s 489C: restriction on appointment of the auditor of a private company which is a public interest entity`

-- the four years begin on the day after the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the first day of the period of 4 years` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS Date 1 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the last day of the period of 4 years` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS Date 31 12 2028
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the first day of the period of 4 years` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 1 3 2024
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the last day of the period of 4 years` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2028  -- four years beginning 1 March 2024 end on the day before 1 March 2028, which is 29 February 2028 (a leap year)
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the last day of the period of 4 years` (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2029
-- s 489C(1) arguments: private PIE, auditor for every year of the period, last day of the maximum engagement period, first day of the proposed year, Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the first day of the four years
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 31 12 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the last day of the four years
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a year that begins after the four years
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a year that begins before the four years
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not auditor for every year of the period
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not a public interest entity
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` NOTHING TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- public interest entity not known
#ASSERT `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- subsection (3): an Auditor General
-- s 489C(2) arguments: private PIE, the auditor of subsection (1) was auditor for every year, the person is of the same network, dates, Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- outside the four years
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not of that network
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the auditor mentioned in (1) was not in that position
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not a public interest entity
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an Auditor General

§§ `s 490: default power of the Secretary of State`

#ASSERT `s 490(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more persons to fill the vacancy` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more persons to fill the vacancy` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no failure: the power is not given; not covered
-- s 490(2) arguments: section 489(2) applies, the company fails to make the necessary appointment
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- it made the appointment in time
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the company's first financial year: subsection (2) of section 489 does not apply
-- the accounts meeting ended on 12 October 2025: one week runs to 19 October 2025
-- arguments: the day the accounts meeting ended, the day the notice was given, the day now
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` (Date 12 10 2025) (JUST (Date 19 10 2025)) (Date 30 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the seventh day after the end
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` (Date 12 10 2025) (JUST (Date 20 10 2025)) (Date 30 10 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the eighth day
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` (Date 12 10 2025) (JUST (Date 13 10 2025)) (Date 30 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` (Date 12 10 2025) NOTHING (Date 19 10 2025) EQUALS NOTHING  -- no notice yet and the week has not run
#ASSERT `s 490(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` (Date 12 10 2025) NOTHING (Date 20 10 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no notice and the week has run
-- the duty as a regulative rule (day 0 is the end of the accounts meeting): expected FULFILLED, BREACH, BREACH
#TRACE `s 490(2) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 490(2) give notice to the Secretary of State of his power having become exercisable` AT 7
#TRACE `s 490(2) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 490(2) give notice to the Secretary of State of his power having become exercisable` AT 8
#TRACE `s 490(2) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)
-- the offence: arguments: the company failed to give the notice
#ASSERT `s 490(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490(3)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not an officer in default
#ASSERT `s 490(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the company gave the notice
#ASSERT `s 490(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING  -- section 1121 not known
-- the penalty: summary conviction only, level 3 and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 3, no imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 490(4) the penalty for an offence under section 490` EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
-- pounds: the amount of level 3 is an input (an arbitrary 1000 is used here to show the arithmetic)
#ASSERT `s 490(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 490(4) the most the person can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 100

§§ `s 490A: defective appointments`

#ASSERT `s 490A(1) the Secretary of State may appoint another auditor or auditors in place of the auditor or auditors appointed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490A(1) the Secretary of State may appoint another auditor or auditors in place of the auditor or auditors appointed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no breach: the power is not given
#ASSERT `s 490A(1) the Secretary of State may appoint another auditor or auditors in place of the auditor or auditors appointed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490A(2) the breach invalidates the report` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "does not invalidate any report"
#ASSERT `s 490A(2) the breach invalidates the report` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- another report: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 490A(3) sections 1248 and 1249 apply as if the auditor was not an appropriate person for the period during which the audit was conducted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490A(3) sections 1248 and 1249 apply as if the auditor was not an appropriate person for the period during which the audit was conducted` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a breach of section 489A or 485B only
-- s 490A(4): the company became aware on 1 March 2025: one week runs to 8 March 2025
-- arguments: the day the company became aware, the day the notice was given, the day now
#ASSERT `s 490A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 9 3 2025)) (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) NOTHING (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` NOTHING NOTHING (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING  -- the company is not yet aware
-- expected: FULFILLED (day 7), BREACH (day 8)
#TRACE `s 490A(4) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of becoming aware of the breach` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 490A(4) give notice to the Secretary of State that the power under subsection (1) has become exercisable` AT 7
#TRACE `s 490A(4) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of becoming aware of the breach` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 490A(4) give notice to the Secretary of State that the power under subsection (1) has become exercisable` AT 8
#ASSERT `s 490A(5)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490A(5)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490A(5)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490A(5)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490A(5)(b) the officer commits an offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490A(5)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490A(6) the penalty for an offence under section 490A` EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490A(6) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 2000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `s 490A(6) the most the person can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` 2000 EQUALS 200

§§ `s 491: term of office`

#ASSERT `s 491(1)(a) the auditor or auditors cannot yet take office` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the previous auditors have not ceased to hold office
#ASSERT `s 491(1)(a) the auditor or auditors cannot yet take office` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- they have ceased: the bar is over
-- s 491(1)(b) arguments: the accounts meeting next following their appointment has concluded, re-appointed
#ASSERT `s 491(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- "at the conclusion of the accounts meeting next following their appointment"
#ASSERT `s 491(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- that meeting has not concluded
#ASSERT `s 491(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "unless re-appointed"
#ASSERT `s 491(2) the term of office rule prejudices the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 491(2) the term of office rule prejudices the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
